  "title": "CHAPTER 11: PUBLIC FINANCE IN INDIA",
  "order": 231,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "grett7k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. MEANING OF PUBLIC FINANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Public Finance examines government revenue, public expenditure, debt management, and budgetary processes in India.",
        "The Finance Commission is constituted under Article 280 every 5 years to determine vertical and horizontal tax devolution between the Centre and States.",
        "Central Sector Schemes are 100% funded and implemented by the Central Government, whereas Centrally Sponsored Schemes involve cost-sharing with States.",
        "Fiscal policy tools regulate economic stability through taxation, public debt sustainability analysis, and targeted subsidies."
      ],
      "id": "8a70vh4"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
