    {
      "id": "dhe4rcl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. PUBLIC DEBT SUSTAINABILITY ANALYSIS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fjg0f67",
      "content": "Debt sustainability refers to government's ability to service debt without crisis."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The term 'Budget' is not explicitly used in the Constitution of India; it is designated as the 'Annual Financial Statement' under Article 112.",
        "Distinguish clearly between Central Sector Schemes (100% Union funded) and Centrally Sponsored Schemes (cost-shared ratio such as 60:40 or 90:10) for prelims questions.",
        "Finance Commission tax devolution criteria include income distance, population, forest cover, demographic performance, and tax effort."
      ],
      "id": "096pykr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1glmc0n",
      "content": "Key Indicators:<br></br>• Debt-to-GDP Ratio<br></br>• Interest Payments / Revenue Receipts<br></br>• Fiscal Deficit as % of GDP<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yyastcc",
      "content": "FRBM 2018 Target: Combined Debt = 60% of GDP (40% Centre, 20% States)."
    },
    {
      "id": "p0p20wr",
